From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH 0157] sweet amfi: answer ExtensionKit bootarg state 0x60 with 0x86 (B14)

ExtensionKit asks AMFI policy syscall 0x60 (query_bootarg_state) before it
registers app extension points. Our stand-in returned 0 without writing the
out value, so ExtensionKit read 0 and insisted on the AMFI IOKit service,
which does not exist on this port: LaunchServices then refused every app
extension ("does not correspond to a known extension point"), pkd could not
make records, and PosterBoard had no poster provider (sig 5 on the old
roots). sunfish 0123 fixes it by returning 0x86.

Additive: only call 0x60 is affected; 0x5a (DYLD policy) and the generic
"return 0 without touching the output" path are unchanged. Logs once:
"SWEET AMFI: bootarg state 0x86 for ExtensionKit".

Verification belongs to B14 (after the B4/B13 root with registered appex
and LaunchServices): expect no "Received 0 extensions", PosterBoard finds a
provider, widget gallery stops waiting.
---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
index a50fca4..98c820e 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
@@ -377,6 +377,16 @@ sweet_sandbox_syscall(struct proc *p, int call, user_addr_t arg)
  */
 #define SWEET_AMFI_CHECK_DYLD_POLICY    0x5a
 #define SWEET_AMFI_DYLD_ALLOW_ALL       0xffULL
+/*
+ * ExtensionKit asks AMFI for the boot-arg state before it registers app
+ * extension points (sunfish 0123). With an all-zero answer it insists on an
+ * AMFI IOKit service that does not exist here, LaunchServices then refuses
+ * every extension ("does not correspond to a known extension point"), pkd
+ * makes no records and PosterBoard has no poster provider. 0x86 keeps the
+ * extension path open without any signature check (this AMFI is a stand-in).
+ */
+#define SWEET_AMFI_QUERY_BOOTARG_STATE  0x60
+#define SWEET_AMFI_BOOTARG_STATE        0x86ULL
 
 static int
 sweet_amfi_syscall(__unused struct proc *p, int call, user_addr_t arg)
@@ -385,6 +395,15 @@ sweet_amfi_syscall(__unused struct proc *p, int call, user_addr_t arg)
 	uint64_t allow = SWEET_AMFI_DYLD_ALLOW_ALL;
 	int error;
 
+	if (call == SWEET_AMFI_QUERY_BOOTARG_STATE) {
+		static bool logged;
+		uint64_t state = SWEET_AMFI_BOOTARG_STATE;
+		if (!logged) {
+			logged = true;
+			printf("SWEET AMFI: bootarg state 0x86 for ExtensionKit\n");
+		}
+		return copyout(&state, arg, sizeof(state));
+	}
 	if (call != SWEET_AMFI_CHECK_DYLD_POLICY) {
 		static uint64_t seen;
 		if (call >= 0 && call < 64 && !(seen & (1ULL << call))) {
